                                                "sense_id": "b082b833-59cb-31ac-928b-9d3d5f819e0e",
                                                "text": "This grand ceremony was immediately followed by a proclamation expreſsly forbidding the Abyſſine clergy, monks, and prieſts, to perform any prieſtly functions till they were previouſly examined and approved by the patriarch ; there being ſome reaſon to doubt whether they had been lawfully examined."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec7f9eca-a0f8-4056-9b4d-86f2becc32c9",
                                                "sense_id": "b082b833-59cb-31ac-928b-9d3d5f819e0e",
                                                "text": "He was sent to Guantánamo in 2002, and Judge Kollar-Kotelly found that from the beginning of his stay, “there is no evidence in the record that anyone directed any allegations toward al-Rabiah nor any indication that interrogators believed al-Rabiah had engaged in any conduct that made him lawfully detainable.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
